  "major": "Allied Health - BHCLR Completion Options",
  "notes": "PARTNERSHIP: The Histotechnology, Sleep Technology, and Surgical Technology options are offered through a partnership with Baptist Health College Little Rock (BHCLR); the professional curriculum (certificate) is taught at BHCLR and transfers in as a block. This completion option is ONLY for students who have completed a BHCLR certificate in Histotechnology, Sleep Technology, or Surgical Technology. UA-PTC residency requirement: at least 25% or 15 credit hours must be completed at UA-PTC. This program of study is 60-64 credit hours with a 2.00 GPA required. CREDIT-RANGE HANDLING: the certificate transfers as 37-49 credits and the gen-ed semesters are listed as 10-14 and 9-13 hours; lower bounds are used per collection rule, giving a mapped total of 60 (certificate 37 + gen-ed 23). Students are admitted into the professional core through the admission/selection criteria of the affiliated school. Additional courses may be required if minimum placement test requirements are not met.",
